ion {:value "1999"} "30 kilometres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "2000"} "50 kilometres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "2005"} "5 kilometres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2006"} "10 kilometres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2007"} "20 kilometres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008"} "4 × 5 kilometres Relay, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "1897"} "1936"] "\n" [:option {:value "1903"} "1948"] "\n" [:option {:value "1909"} "1952"] "\n" [:option {:value "1917"} "1956"] "\n" [:option {:value "1928"} "1960"] "\n" [:option {:value "1939"} "1964"] "\n" [:option {:value "1951"} "1968"] "\n" [:option {:value "1963"} "1972"] "\n" [:option {:value "1975"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "1988"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "2015"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "2032"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "2052"} "1994"] "\n" [:option {:value "2072"} "1998"] "\n" [:option {:value "2104"} "2002"] "\n" [:option {:value "2148"} "2006"] "\n" [:option {:value "923569"} "2010"] "\n" [:option {:value "350069"} "2014"] "\n" [:option {:value "9000280"} "2018"] "\n" [:option {:value "19019715"} "2022"] "\n" [:option {:value "15000136"} "2026"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/191"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "4 × 10 kilometres Relay, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "16 February 1984 — 8:45"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/124"} "Veliko Polje, Igman"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/2001"} "68 from 17 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {:valign "top"} "Details"] [:td {} "Course Length: ?" [:br {}] "Height Differential: 122 m" [:br {}] "Maximum Climb: 36 m" [:br {}] "Total Climbing: 363 m"]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The men’s relay race at the 1982 World Championships in Oslo turned out to be the most dramatic race in the history of cross-country skiing to this date. On the last leg, a few hundred meters from the finish, the Soviet Union’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/99184"} "Aleksandr Zavyalov"] " and Norway’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/84436"} "Oddvar Brå"] " were close together. Zavalyov fell, but Brå broke one of his poles, only to get a new one quickly, and they skiied side-by-side over the last meters. The race was judged a draw, and for the first time there two world champion relay teams. And that was not the end of the story. Finland and Eastern Germany had a close fight for the bronze, and the judges could not separate them either, as they shared bronze. Ties for first and third, a unique feat."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The defending Olympic Champion Soviet Union was favored to win another Olympic relay gold, but a close competition was expected with Finland and Sweden. On the first leg, Sweden’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/98835"} "Thomas Wassberg"] " had a 10 second lead over the Soviet Union’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/83898"} "Aleksandr Batyuk"] ", with US skier " [:a {:href "/athletes/97557"} "Dan Simoneau"] " in a surprising third. Norway in sixth and Finland in eighth position were left far behind. On the second leg, the Soviet Union’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/99184"} "Aleksandr Zavyalov"] " passed Sweden’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/88098"} "Benny Kohlberg"] " and sent " [:a {:href "/athletes/95844"} "Vladimir Nikitin"] " out on the third leg with a 12 second lead over Sweden’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/96109"} "Jan Ottosson"] ". " [:a {:href "/athletes/95428"} "Juha Mieto"] " brought Finland back in the fight for the medals by bringing his team up to third place, half a second ahead of Norway, but over 1½ minutes behind the leading Soviet team. Ottoson was able to close the gap to Nikitin, and was only half a second behind at the last exchange. Norway’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/83751"} "Ove Aunli"] ", third at the last exchange, was 10 seconds ahead of Finland’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/87989"} "Harri Kirvesniemi"] ". The last leg saw a close duel between the two 1984 Olympic champions, " [:a {:href "/athletes/98002"} "Gunde Svan"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/99245"} "Nikolay Zimyatov"] ". The young Swede left his Russian rival and secured Sweden their first Olympic relay gold medal since 1964. Finland’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/87811"} "Aki Karvonen"] " had an easy contest for the bronze medal against Norway’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/86745"} "Tor Håkon Holte"] ", leaving the Norwegian almost one minute behind."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {} "Exchange"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "5"] [:td {} "Sweden"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SWE.png"}] "SWE"]] [:td {} "1-55:06.3"] [:td {} "– (–)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "Lead-Off"] [:td {:class "bib"} "5-1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/98835"} "Thomas Wassberg"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "28:47.0"] [:td {} "28:47.0 (1)"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2nd Leg"] [:td {:class "bib"} "5-2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/88098"} "Benny Kohlberg"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "28:47.9"] [:td {} "57:34.9 (2)"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3rd Leg"] [:td {:class "bib"} "5-3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/96109"} "Jan Ottosson"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "29:04.1"] [:td {}